<newsitem itemid="147149" id="root" date="1996-10-28" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Engen year earnings soar after poor 1995.</title>
<headline>Engen year earnings soar after poor 1995.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Aug 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     218	   vs 73</p>
<p>    Shr pre-exceps (cts)  202	   vs 118</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 96	    vs 60</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   436	   vs 142</p>
<p>    Net income		349	   vs 116</p>
<p>    Tax			 80	    vs 14</p>
<p>    Turnover		10,870.0	vs 9,004.0</p>
<p>Div payable December 20</p>
<p>on register November 15</p>
<p>Full name: Engen Ltd</p>
<p>    Exceptional items    31 gain	vs 79 loss</p>
<p>NOTE - Oil and fuels firm Engen said that the 1996 tax figure included a transfer to a tax equalisation reserve of 63 million rand, compared to 25 million rand in 1995.</p>
<p>Analysts polled by Reuters had forecast earnings per share of 200 to 220 cents and a dividend of 90 to 110 cents.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
